Milestone 2: MFE/MAE Tracking Engine
Depends on: Milestone 1. Effort: Medium.

Summary
No changes to the core MFE/MAE logic. It operates per-trade, using that trade’s instrument_settings for spread adjustment. Each trade stores its own bar_close_r[], bar_high_r[], bar_low_r[] arrays.

The only multi-instrument consideration: when processing background trades (trades on instruments not currently displayed), the engine reads bar data from the correct dataset for that trade’s ticker. This is already handled by the time-sync logic in Milestone 1.

All other details (exit-bar clamping, TF locking, entry bar exclusion, SL/TP modification logging, floating PnL for equity) remain identical. Refer to the previous milestone document.

