Milestone 8: Polish & Edge Cases
Depends on: All previous. Effort: Medium.

8.1 Chart Switching While Trades Are Open
When the user switches from EURUSD chart to GBPUSD chart, the GBPUSD chart must jump to the session’s current_time. Any GBPUSD trades that exist should be visible on the chart with correct entry/exit lines and floating PnL.

8.2 Notification System for Background Trades
When a trade on a background instrument (not currently displayed) hits TP, SL, or margin stop-out, show a notification banner: “GBPUSD Long 0.3L closed at TP (+1.8R, +$54.00).” The user can click the notification to switch to that instrument’s chart.

8.3 Open Positions Panel
A collapsible panel showing all open trades across all instruments: ticker, direction, lot size, floating PnL ($ and R), margin used, time in trade. Clicking a row switches the chart to that instrument.

8.4 Multiple Trades on Same Instrument
The user can have multiple trades on the same pair (e.g., two separate EURUSD longs with different entries and SLs). Each is tracked independently. The instrument filter in the dashboard aggregates them.

8.5 Margin Across Hedged Positions
If the user goes long EURUSD and also short EURUSD, some brokers reduce margin (hedging). For simplicity in version 1, do NOT model hedged margin reduction. Both positions require full margin. Add hedged margin as a future enhancement.

8.6 All Previous Edge Cases
All edge cases from the previous revision still apply: skip/fast-forward integrity (process every bar on every active instrument), entry bar exclusion, breakeven stop, partial close with margin release, SL/TP modifications, undo/redo, session reset.

